  "query_preview": "..\n\nNext 7 days (through next Sunday)...\n\nSplit troffing will be over the area today. This will keep\nisolated to scattered showers, and a few embedded thunderstorms, \nin the forecast through early evening. Outside of far southeast\nMontana, none of this activity is expected to be very substantial.\nThere is a slight chance for a strong storm or two late\nafternoon/early evening along the eastern state line counties\n(Fallon/Carter), but models are keeping the majority of the\nstronger activity east of Montana. Monday night drier air will\nbuild in from the west as the weak trof aloft exits to the east.\nThis will bring an end to precipitation chances across the region\nby late evening. \n\nModels continue to advertise a mild and mainly dry forecast for \nthe week ahead. There have been a couple of weak cool air \nintrusions added into the models over the past 24 hours. One \narrives Wednesday as a weak dry cold front, and a similar \nsituation develops for Saturday. Ahead of the Wednesday front, \nforecast high temperatures on Tuesday have increased into the mid \nto upper 70s with a few lower 80s not out of the question. Behind \nthe front Wednesday, highs drop about 10 degrees back to around \n70. Highs for the rest of the week into the weekend range between \n65 and 75 degrees with a lot of sunshine and dry conditions. \nExpect breezy conditions in the afternoon Tuesday and Wednesday \nacross western (Livingston, Big Timber, Harlowton) and northern \n(Harlowton to Baker) portions of the forecast area. Chambers",
